     "text": "In October 2013, hedge fund founder Ray Dalio released a thirty minute animated cartoon. You think global economics requires advanced math and complex banking degrees, but Dalio proved the entire system is just a mechanical engine. He founded Bridgewater Associates, which grew into the largest hedge fund in the world. His video illustrates money as a flowing river cascading over a water wheel. That constant stream drives production in a simple circular loop. Every buyer transaction powers the gear. So the massive global market runs on basic mechanics. A cartoon explains it better than a textbook."
